From: Christoph Berliner <32103696+Styx85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:15:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/11] HIP: use the gfx900 dp4a asm sequence also for
 gfx909/gfx90c

gfx909 and gfx90c share the gfx900 ISA (no dot instructions) but fell through
to the generic C++ dp4a fallback. clang emits similar instructions, but the
register allocation of the MMQ kernels is much worse: on gfx90c
mul_mat_q<Q4_K, 64> spilled 431 VGPRs (912 B scratch per lane), mmq_x 32 290.
With the asm sequence: 30 resp. 0 spilled VGPRs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
index 17e1bd3..9fc0d0f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-cuda/common.cuh
@@ -765,7 +765,9 @@ static __device__ __forceinline__ int ggml_cuda_dp4a(const int a, const int b, i
     c = __builtin_amdgcn_sdot4(a, b, c, false);
 #elif defined(RDNA3) || defined(RDNA4_M) || defined(RDNA4)
     c = __builtin_amdgcn_sudot4( true, a, true, b, c, false);
-#elif defined(RDNA1) || defined(__gfx900__)
+#elif defined(RDNA1) || defined(__gfx900__) || defined(__gfx909__) || defined(__gfx90c__)
+    // gfx909/gfx90c have the gfx900 ISA. Besides being explicit, the asm block keeps register pressure in
+    // check: with the generic C++ fallback the MMQ kernels spill hundreds of VGPRs on these GPUs.
     int tmp1;
     int tmp2;
     asm("\n \
